        "description": "Give password (text). It is scored as the sign-in pages score it as it is typed (password-strength.mjs, passwords.json): 0 when shorter than min_length (8), then 1, plus one for 12 characters or more and one for three kinds of character (lower case, upper case, digits, others). Answers score, said (the words for that score), min_length, max_length and too_long (whether the service would refuse it as longer than max_length). The password is judged in memory only: it is never printed back, kept or sent, and nothing is signed in, made or changed. The sign-in pages themselves (passkey.mjs, kept in this folder but not run here) do the rest of the old job: they run the passkey step through the browser's WebAuthn, send and check emailed codes and post the email-and-password form; those need a browser and the sign-in service, which this run does not have.",
